n(NULL)` ⇒ **SIGSEGV** | `crash_35_stralloc_null_str` |\n| 36 | `stbds_strreset` (lib.c:924) | all-zero arena (`storage == NULL`) — the empty case | loop body never runs, arena zeroed, returns | `err_36_strreset_empty` |\n| 37 | `stbds_strreset` | `a == NULL` | `a->storage` read from address 0 ⇒ **SIGSEGV** | `crash_37_strreset_null` |\n| 38 | `strkey` (lib.c:941) | `INT_MIN` / `INT_MAX` (widest `%d` expansion, 17 bytes incl. NUL) | fits the 256-byte static buffer, no overflow | `err_38_strkey_extremes` |\n| 39 | `helxo` (lib.h) | `letter` = `0`, `0x80..0xFF` (negative `char`), `'\\n'` | printed verbatim by `%c`; byte-identical stdout required | `err_39_helxo_all_bytes` |\n| 40 | `stbds_hmput_key` / `stbds_hmget_key` (lib.c:596/719) | key whose `stbds_hash_*` result is `0` or `1` (the reserved EMPTY/DELETED hashes) | `if (hash < 2) hash += 2;` — remapped, no error | `err_40_reserved_hash_values` |\n| 41 | `stbds_shmode_func` (lib.c:803) | `mode` out of the `STBDS_SH_*` enum range, e.g. `-1`, `256`, `INT_MAX` | `(unsigned char)mode` truncation ⇒ `string.mode = 255/0/255`; subsequent `put` takes the binary `default:` branch | `err_41_shmode_out_of_range` |\n| 42 | `stbds_hmput_key` (lib.c:686) | `a == NULL` (implicit map creation) + `elemsize == 0` (degenerate) | `ARR_TO_HASH == HASH_TO_ARR == a`; insert still succeeds with `temp = 0`, `memcpy(...,0)` | `err_42_put_zero_elemsize` |\n\n## Notes\n\n* Rows 20–23, 25, 31 are asserts that cannot be triggered through the exported API.\n  They are nevertheless **replicated verbatim in the Rust translation** (calling\n  `abort()` through the same `__assert_fail` libc entry point) so that a future\n  caller that does reach them observes the same `SIGABRT` instead of Rust UB.\n* Crash rows (2, 4, 5, 24, 33, 35, 37) are compared in a **child process**\n  (`tests/phase_c_crash.rs`): the child loads exactly one of the two libraries,\n  performs the operation, and the parent compares the wait-status (exit code /\n  fatal signal) of