{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_26lpgjo5xhtkxu7grevwjpvnvm46jnlzdnvzm4wbn7joiofv3qiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016ymixqugkUw3c5T8TxZiVh","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-c7KYZo/translation/ERRORS.md","old_string":"* Rows 20–23, 25, 31 are asserts that cannot be triggered through the exported API.\n  They are nevertheless **replicated verbatim in the Rust translation** (calling\n  `abort()` through the same `__assert_fail` libc entry point) so that a future\n  caller that does reach them observes the same `SIGABRT` instead of Rust UB.\n* Crash rows (2, 4, 5, 24, 33, 35, 37) are compared in a **child process**\n  (`tests/phase_c_crash.rs`): the child loads exactly one of the two libraries,\n  performs the operation, and the parent compares the wait-status (exit code /\n  fatal signal) of the C child against the Rust child. Assert/abort text on stderr\n  differs only in the recorded `__FILE__` path of the build, which is not a\n  property of the translation.","new_string":"* Rows 20–23, 25, 31 are asserts that cannot be triggered through the exported API.\n  They are nevertheless **replicated verbatim in the Rust translation** (same\n  expression text, function name and line number, raised through the same libc\n  `__assert_fail` entry point) so that a caller that does reach them observes the\n  same `SIGABRT` instead of Rust UB. Row 24 proves this works end to end: both\n  libraries die with `SIGABRT` **and** the same `Assertion \\`slot >= 0' failed`\n  text (only the recorded `__FILE__` path differs, which is a property of the\n  build tree, not of the translation).\n* Crash rows are compared in a **child process** (`tests/phase_c_crash.rs`): the\n  child loads exactly one of the two libraries, performs the operation, and the\n  parent compares the wait-status (exit code / fatal signal) and the assertion\n  text. A surviving child exits with code 7, so \"survived\" can never be confused\n  with a signal death or a libtest failure (101).\n* Observed results (both profiles):\n\n  | scenario | C | Rust |\n  |----------|---|------|\n  | `control_survive`, `arrgrowf_size_overflow`, `hash_bytes_null_len0`, `hmfree_func_null`, `hmdel_key_null_map` | exit 7 | exit 7 |\n  | `arrgrowf_oom`, `arrfreef_null`, `hash_string_null`, `hash_bytes_null_len1`, `hash_bytes_huge_len`, `stralloc_forged_arena`, `stralloc_null_str`, `stralloc_huge_block`, `strreset_null`, `hmput_key_null_key_bin`, `hmput_key_null_key_str`, `hmget_key_ts_null_temp`, `hmput_key_huge_keysize` | SIGSEGV | SIGSEGV |\n  | `hmdel_ptr_to_string` | SIGABRT + `slot >= 0` | SIGABRT + `slot >= 0` |\n* `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` is required for this parity: libstd's\n  debug assertions would turn the C's *deliberate* UB paths (a write through\n  `NULL + sizeof(header)`) into a Rust panic, so the dev profile would report\n  `SIGABRT` where the C reports `SIGSEGV`. With it, the dev and release cdylibs\n  behave identically and both match the C."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1327,"cache_read_input_tokens":263089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1327,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53cdfebf-584b-400d-8e8a-413b0712cc6f","uuid":"d2f1a6a2-d744-4179-b0ee-334bf414fda9","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:13:55.358Z"}
