{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a97734d8f217c7da5","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JJyP2TEcbhMoNNeJZEP6kw","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-OaoIk6/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-c7KYZo/53cdfebf-584b-400d-8e8a-413b0712cc6f/tasks/a97734d8f217c7da5.output","summary":"## Result\n\nI read both files in full, compared all 24 functions line-by-line, and then validated the analysis empirically by `dlopen`-ing both shared objects (`c_src/build/libharvest-work-c7KYZo.so` and `translation/target/release/libhelxo_lib.so`) in one process and diffing byte-exact state traces.\n\n### Per-function verdicts\n\n- OK: `stbds_arrgrowf` (min_len wrap, `min_cap<=cap` early return preserving pointer identity, `2*cap` vs `<4` ladder, `realloc(NULL,…)` for `a==NULL`, header field writes only on the NULL path, `capacity` written last)\n- OK: `stbds_arrfreef`\n- OK: `stbds_rand_seed`\n- OK: `stbds_load_32_or_64` (`v64_lo ^ v32` computed in 32-bit then zero-extended; `<<16<<16>>16>>16` identity; yields `a=0x27bb2ee687b0b0fd`, `b=0xb504f32d` in both)\n- OK: `stbds_probe_position`\n- OK: `stbds_log2`\n- OK: `stbds_make_hash_index` (`sizeof(stbds_hash_index)==104`, `sizeof(stbds_hash_bucket)==128`, `t+1` = +104 bytes, `ALIGN_FWD` to 64, threshold arithmetic, `string` copied as 24 raw bytes incl. padding, seed LCG update order, `goto done` == `break 'outer` so the `j` loop continues)\n- OK: `stbds_hash_string` (`(unsigned char)*str++`, `hash^=hash^ror(...)` idiom, all wrapping)\n- OK: `stbds_siphash_bytes` — including the two int-overflow/sign-extension quirks: `d[0]|(d[1]<<8)|(d[2]<<16)|(d[3]<<24)` sign-extends into `size_t` (Rust: `w0 as i64 as usize`), the `(size_t)(...)<<16<<16` cast-before-shift, and the `switch(len-i)` fall-through modelled as descending `if rem >= n`\n- OK: `stbds_hash_bytes`\n- OK: `stbds_is_key_equal` (`i` reinterpreted as `size_t` for `elemsize*i`)\n- OK: `stbds_hmfree_func`\n- OK: `stbds_hm_find_slot` (`pos & ~7` via `!7usize`, both inner loops, `-1` on `HASH_EMPTY`)\n- OK: `stbds_hmget_key_ts` (NULL path order: `length+=1` → `memset` → `*temp`)\n- OK: `stbds_hmget_key`\n- OK: `stbds_hmput_default`\n- OK: `stbds_hmput_key` — including the different NULL-path order (`memset` **before** `length+=1`, unlike `hmget_key_ts`), `string.mode` set on `nt` before publishing `hash_table`, and the original stb bug that the **wrap-around** inner loop (C 746–759 / Rust 890–914) does *not* set `stbds_temp_key`. I exercised that path 701 times out of 3000 re-puts; both libraries agreed exactly.\n- OK: `stbds_shmode_func`\n- OK: `stbds_hmdel_key` (`final_index = len-2`, `free` without `keyoffset` at C:837, `find_slot` **with** `keyoffset` at C:843/845, shrink-vs-rebuild `else if`, `length-=1` placement). The omitted `assert(table->used_count >= 0)` at C:832 is correct: it is always true for `size_t` and gcc compiled it out — no such string exists in the C `.so`.\n- OK: `stbds_strdup`\n- OK: `stbds_stralloc` (`sizeof(*sb)-8` = 8, `512 << (block>>1)` with x86 6-bit shift masking via `wrapping_shl`, the `len>blocksize` branch that links the oversize block *after* the head and sets `remaining=0` only when `storage==NULL`, and the `p = storage->storage + remaining - len` order)\n- OK: `stbds_strreset`\n- OK: `strkey`\n- OK: `helxo` — the C passes the whole 16-byte `{char*; char}` struct as a variadic argument; per SysV it occupies two INTEGER registers, so `%s` reads `key` and `%c` reads the low byte of the second eightbyte. Passing `(key, value as c_int)` is ABI-equivalent; verified identical stdout for `letter` = `'o'`, `'x'`, `'!'`, `0`, `(char)-1`, `'Z'`.\n\n### The one divergence found\n\n**`STBDS_ASSERT` message text on stderr** (affects every live assert site).\n\n- C: `lib.c:3` `#define STBDS_ASSERT assert`, expanded at **lib.c:401, 778, 828, 846, 849, 913**\n- Rust: macro at **lib.rs:52–63**, invoked at **lib.rs:361, 936, 1021, 1075, 1083, 1171**\n\nTwo differences in the arguments handed to `__assert_fail`:\n\n1. `function`: glibc's `assert` passes `__ASSERT_FUNCTION` (= `__PRETTY_FUNCTION__`), which **in C is the bare identifier**. The C `.so`'s `.rodata` contains exactly `stbds_make_hash_index`, `stbds_hmput_key`, `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_stralloc`. The Rust passes C++-style signatures (`lib.rs:368, 940, 1025, 1079, 1087, 1175`), e.g. `void *stbds_hmdel_key(void *, size_t, void *, size_t, size_t, int)`. This mismatch is unconditional.\n2. `file`: C passes `__FILE__`, which for this CMake build is the absolute path `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-c7KYZo/c_src/src/lib.c` (present verbatim in the C `.so`). Rust hardcodes `\"c_src/src/lib.c\"` (`lib.rs:57`).\n\nThe assert *expression* strings and *line numbers* match exactly, and the abort behaviour (SIGABRT, rc=134) matches.\n\nConcrete reproducer (deterministic, no randomness):\n\n```c\nstruct { char *key; char value; } *t = NULL;                 /* elemsize 16 */\nstbds_rand_seed(0x31415926);\nt = stbds_hmput_key(t, 16, \"aa\", 8, 2);   /* mode = 2, i.e. >= STBDS_HM_STRING */\nt = stbds_hmput_key(t, 16, \"bb\", 8, 2);\nt = stbds_hmput_key(t, 16, \"cc\", 8, 2);\nt = stbds_hmdel_key(t, 16, \"aa\", 8, 0, 2);   /* hits assert(slot >= 0) at lib.c:846 */\n```\n\n(`mode >= 2` makes `hmdel_key` take the `else` branch at C:845 and hash the *address* of the key field instead of the key string — a genuine upstream stb\\_ds bug, faithfully reproduced. `mode = 3` behaves the same.) Observed:\n\n```\nC:    m2: /local/.../c_src/src/lib.c:846: stbds_hmdel_key: Assertion `slot >= 0' failed.\nRust: m2: c_src/src/lib.c:846: void *stbds_hmdel_key(void *, size_t, void *, size_t, size_t, int): Assertion `slot >= 0' failed.\n```\n\n### Differential test coverage backing the \"OK\" verdicts\n\nAll runs compared with `cmp` (byte-exact), including full hash-bucket dumps (`hash[]`/`index[]` for every slot), all `stbds_hash_index` fields, array headers, raw element memory, `temp_key`, arena block-list lengths, and exit codes:\n\n| suite | volume | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `hash_string`/`hash_bytes` (7 seeds × lens 0–48, all-0xFF/0x80/0x7F fills, single high byte at each of 16 positions) | 1567 lines | identical |\n| `arrgrowf` ladders incl. `elemsize=0`, `min_cap=0` | 159 | identical |\n| `hmput_default` incl. forced `length==0` path | 5 | identical |\n| binary maps n=1..8, 40, 200, 500 (grow, rehash, delete, shrink, rebuild) | 57 399 | identical |\n| 8-byte keys, string maps, `shmode` 0/1/2/3, keyoffset≠0, mode 1/2/3, NULL-input entry points, tombstone reuse | ~15 000 | identical |\n| `stralloc` random lengths (2400 allocs) + `block` byte 0–255 + exact-fit boundaries 500–525 | 2528 | identical |\n| randomized stress: 20 trials × 4000 mixed put/delete over 600 keys, slot_count up to 1024 | 124 538 lines / 6.73 MB | identical |\n| `strkey`, `helxo` (6 `letter` values, stdout captured) | 46 | identical |\n\nEvery crash/abort my harness provoked (SIGSEGV rc=139, SIGABRT rc=134) occurred at the identical point in both libraries with identical preceding output. Note the Rust `Cargo.toml` disables `overflow-checks`/`debug-assertions` in **both** profiles, so the non-`wrapping_*` arithmetic that remains in `lib.rs` also wraps like C.\n\nNo files were modified.","usage":{"total_tokens":178390,"tool_uses":29,"duration_ms":1196242},"uuid":"f26350dd-d6c9-4cf9-b58d-6dc69ab61a3d","session_id":"53cdfebf-584b-400d-8e8a-413b0712cc6f"}
