 5 | identical |\n| binary maps n=1..8, 40, 200, 500 (grow, rehash, delete, shrink, rebuild) | 57 399 | identical |\n| 8-byte keys, string maps, `shmode` 0/1/2/3, keyoffset≠0, mode 1/2/3, NULL-input entry points, tombstone reuse | ~15 000 | identical |\n| `stralloc` random lengths (2400 allocs) + `block` byte 0–255 + exact-fit boundaries 500–525 | 2528 | identical |\n| randomized stress: 20 trials × 4000 mixed put/delete over 600 keys, slot_count up to 1024 | 124 538 lines / 6.73 MB | identical |\n| `strkey`, `helxo` (6 `letter` values, stdout captured) | 46 | identical |\n\nEvery crash/abort my harness provoked (SIGSEGV rc=139, SIGABRT rc=134) occurred at the identical point in both libraries with identical preceding output. Note the Rust `Cargo.toml` disables `overflow-checks`/`debug-assertions` in **both** profiles, so the non-`wrapping_*` arithmetic that remains in `lib.rs` also wraps like C.\n\nNo files were modified."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":1196244,"totalTokens":182509,"totalToolUseCount":29,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2980,"cache_read_input_tokens":175117,"output_tokens":4410,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1085},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2980},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":2,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":25,"editFileCount":2,"linesAdded":820,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
