{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014LPwXneaaHhqqSiLCXvN2V","type":"tool_result","content":"=== artifacts ===\nCONFIGS.md\nERRORS.md\nSYMBOLS.md\ncheck_features.sh\n\n=== rows documented ===\nCONFIGS.md rows: 85\nERRORS.md rows : 50\nunchecked CONFIGS rows: 0\n\n=== Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"translation\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"helxo_lib\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n# The translation reproduces the C semantics literally: every arithmetic\n# operation that can overflow uses the wrapping form, and the raw pointer\n# arithmetic faithfully reproduces the C's UB paths (e.g. `stbds_arrgrowf`\n# dereferencing `NULL + sizeof(header)` after a failed `realloc`, which the C\n# build resolves as SIGSEGV). libstd's debug assertions would turn those into a\n# Rust panic (SIGABRT), i.e. the dev profile would behave differently from both\n# the release profile and the C library, so they are switched off.\n[profile.dev]\ndebug-assertions = false\noverflow-checks = false\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 3\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53cdfebf-584b-400d-8e8a-413b0712cc6f","uuid":"355bad04-d7a8-416e-b1b0-792382517b12","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:44:14.702Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== artifacts ===\nCONFIGS.md\nERRORS.md\nSYMBOLS.md\ncheck_features.sh\n\n=== rows documented ===\nCONFIGS.md rows: 85\nERRORS.md rows : 50\nunchecked CONFIGS rows: 0\n\n=== Cargo.toml ===\n[package]\nname = \"translation\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"helxo_lib\"\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\npath = \"src/lib.rs\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n\n# The translation reproduces the C semantics literally: every arithmetic\n# operation that can overflow uses the wrapping form, and the raw pointer\n# arithmetic faithfully reproduces the C's UB paths (e.g. `stbds_arrgrowf`\n# dereferencing `NULL + sizeof(header)` after a failed `realloc`, which the C\n# build resolves as SIGSEGV). libstd's debug assertions would turn those into a\n# Rust panic (SIGABRT), i.e. the dev profile would behave differently from both\n# the release profile and the C library, so they are switched off.\n[profile.dev]\ndebug-assertions = false\noverflow-checks = false\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 3\npanic = \"abort\"\n\n[workspace]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uk764tkqniaiu374svy3vjuo47wrjbimxly4xolbzz4plfabs4bq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — all four phases pass.** (The 85 \"CONFIGS rows\" count includes the 50 config rows plus the 35 row→test mapping rows I appended.)\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is one TU embedding **stb_ds**'s implementation (array + hash-map + string-arena) plus `strkey`/`helxo`. 16 exported symbols. `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` is empty ⇒ **`assert()` is live** (the `.so` imports `__assert_fail`) — this drove much of Phase C.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (in `translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — all 16 `nm -D` symbols; C↔Rust diff **empty in both directions** (no stubs needed, no untranslated module).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 50-row error-surface table mechanically grepped from the C: every early-return sentinel, all 6 live asserts (incl. the one gcc folds away), every NULL/zero/oversize/out-of-range-enum path.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 50-row configuration table (mode ∈ ℤ, `string.mode` ∈ 0..255, 3 creation paths, elemsize/keysize/keyoffset shapes, count boundaries 5/6/12/13/24/48/1000, grow/shrink/rebuild/tombstone paths, arena block chain) + row→test mapping.\n\n## Phases B/C — 67 differential tests, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`\nState comparison is a full canonical dump after **every** call: array header, all 9 hash-index fields, arena, **every bucket slot's `hash[]`/`index[]`**, and payload — with fixed-seed randomized inputs per row. Crash rows run in child processes comparing exit code / fatal signal / assert text.\n\n## Divergences found and fixed in the Rust\n1. **Missing live asserts** — the C aborts via `__assert_fail`; Rust did OOB writes instead. Added all 6 with identical expression text, line numbers and bare `__PRETTY_FUNCTION__` names. Reachable case now matches byte-for-byte: `lib.c:846: stbds_hmdel_key: Assertion \\`slot >= 0' failed.` + SIGABRT (found by delegated review, verified against the C `.so`'s `.rodata`).\n2. **`512 << (block>>1)` panicked** in the dev profile for a forged `block ≥ 128` (C/x86 masks the count) → `wrapping_shl`; plus all remaining `+`/`-`/`<<` made explicitly wrapping, and `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false` so dev ≡ release ≡ C on the C's UB paths.\n3. **`t->string = ot->string`** now a 24-byte copy including padding, matching gcc.\n\nTwo test-harness bugs of my own were also fixed (use-after-free read of `capacity`; a non-reentrant mutex deadlock), and one *apparent* divergence turned out to be genuine C behaviour I had mis-modelled: `stbds_hmput_key`'s wrap-around branch deliberately leaves `temp_key` stale — the Rust already replicated it.\n\n**Gate:** symbol diff empty (dev + release) · all 50 CONFIGS rows `[x]` · all 50 ERRORS rows tested · exactly one feature combination (no `[features]`), verified by `./check_features.sh` → `PHASE D: OK`. `c_src/` untouched apart from the required `build/`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":306831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1053,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53cdfebf-584b-400d-8e8a-413b0712cc6f","uuid":"7074dfff-7580-454b-ab10-bc0f44670e8c","timestamp":"2026-08-27T10:44:33.926Z"}
